cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sqlbenchdag: a reproducible SQL benchmarking laboratory"
message: "If you use this software or its published capsules, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ramona C."
    family-names: Truta
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4886-7777"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rctruta/sql-benchmarks-dagster"
url: "https://github.com/rctruta/sql-benchmarks-dagster"
abstract: >-
  A SQL benchmarking laboratory that produces reproducible experiments, not just
  numbers. Every experiment is identified by a content-addressed Experiment ID
  (a hash of its config, SQL, and measurement code) and published as a capsule
  that is integrity-sealed, OpenTimestamps-anchored to Bitcoin, and covered by a
  signed release tag — so any cited result can be re-run and verified without
  trusting the author.
keywords:
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - DuckDB
  - PostgreSQL
  - SQL
  - Dagster
  - data-engineering
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-22"
